diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..86e2cbd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,18 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+The client router keeps up to five visited views mounted, including the active
+view. Inactive views are hidden and inert; revisiting a path and query string
+reuses its DOM and component state. Hash links share the same view. Astro still
+loads each destination to update page metadata and styles, and manages history
+and scroll restoration. The least recently used view is removed when the cache
+is full. Reloading clears the cache. Sign-in and sign-up use `cacheView={false}`
+on `Layout` so their forms are discarded when leaving. Cached content remains a
+snapshot until eviction or reload; data that must stay current should refresh
+on `astro:page-load` and scope DOM queries to the visible route view.
+
+Run the DOM cache tests with `pnpm test` (Node.js 24 or later).
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
